### Health probes. Open in VS Code with the REST Client extension, or in a JetBrains IDE.
### Start the stack and the API first: docker compose up -d --wait, then pnpm --filter @orderpilot/api dev
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Liveness: the process is up. Never touches the database.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### Readiness: 200 when the database, Redis and storage answer, 503 when one is down.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### Health: the status and the name and status of each check. Nothing about the build or the environment.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Send your own request id: it comes back in X-Request-Id and in every log line.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
X-Request-Id: my-first-request-001
